+### [SOAR-based Adaptive Refinement](10020-soar-based-adaptive-refinement.md)
+SOAR-based Adaptive Refinement is a crack-free mesh generation scheme for adaptive subdivision of tetrahedral meshes. It solves the problem of maintaining geometric consistency during incremental refinement by storing object-space error terms and bounding spheres for "diamonds" (pairs of cousin patches). It sets itself apart from static mesh representations by enforcing a strict nesting hierarchy where parent error/sphere values dominate children, and cousins agree on shared values, ensuring that refinement decisions are globally consistent without requiring full mesh reconstruction.
 
